    },
    {
      "line": 16,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "@contract: engain.scene_text_packet.v1"
    },
    {
      "line": 17,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 18,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene 012.1 — the convergence of desperation"
    },
    {
      "line": 20,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "scene meta:"
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "location: Ruins of Central Valley"
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "time: year 10,550, month 1, day 3"
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "participants: Torhh, Korrhan, Saresh, Pazuzu, Giant tribal representatives"
    },
    {
      "line": 24,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "focus: Tribal leaders gather in the ruined central valley to report overwhelming Anunnaki pressure across all fronts; Pazuzu confesses his lingering Anunnaki programming; Torhh invokes the Garden's planetary memory and proposes reaching the Aeon Keepers through the planetary consciousness matrix via Torrhen; the council agrees to seek ancient defense protocols."
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "continuity: 1 year, 8 months, 36 days after the alliance with the Brajor in scene 011.3"
    },
    {
      "line": 26,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "presentation: playable-cutscene"
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "cutscene purpose: The inter-tribal council in the central valley ruins, Pazuzu's confession of Anunnaki programming, Torhh's appeal to the Garden's planetary memory, and the decision to commune with the Aeon Keepers through Torrhen."
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The tribal leaders gathered at the one location all factions could still access: the ruins of what had once been the Garden's central valley, now scarred by millennia of occupation but still carrying faint resonance of the cooperation that had built paradise."
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Torhh represented the Tidecallers—ancient beyond most, memory stretching back to the First Coming and even fragments of the Garden itself."
    },
    {
      "line": 32,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Beside the jade-green Giant stood Korrhan of the Ash Giants, its burnt-red stone-flesh cracked and barely holding cohesion after months of Gruulith assault."
    },
    {
      "line": 33,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Saresh limped forward for the desert tribes, its body fragmenting from sustained Dregan sonic attacks."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Representatives from Forest, Mountain, Highland, and Subterranean populations completed the circle, each bearing wounds that spoke of coordinated Anunnaki pressure across all territories."
    },
    {
      "line": 36,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And among them, Pazuzu—elder of the Igigi, having survived three and a half millennia of slavery, his elongated form diminished by age but consciousness sharper than ever."
    },
    {
      "line": 38,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Korrhan",
      "text": "\"We are losing,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 40,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Saresh",
      "text": "\"The desert is worse,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 42,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Forest Giants reported similar devastation."
    },
    {
      "line": 43,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Highland tribes had lost contact with three settlements entirely."
    },
    {
      "line": 44,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Even the Subterranean populations, protected by depth and darkness, were detecting Anunnaki probes seeking their hidden strongholds."
    },
    {
      "line": 46,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Only the Tidecallers had found unexpected advantage—the Brajor's defection providing aquatic allies rather than additional enemies."
    },
    {
      "line": 47,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But that single bright point in a field of disasters made the other tribes suspicious rather than hopeful."
    },
    {
      "line": 49,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"You ally with Anunnaki creatures while we die,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 50,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "a Mountain Giant rumbled, its charcoal-grey form bearing wounds that spoke of recent combat. \"The ocean-dwellers always claimed they wanted cooperation, yet when we need aid, you're negotiating with the enemy.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 52,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Torhh",
      "text": "\"The Brajor chose alliance,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 54,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Korrhan",
      "text": "\"Convenient distinction,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 56,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Pazuzu's bioluminescence flared—sharp patterns that cut through the rising tensions."
    },
    {
      "line": 57,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"This is exactly what she wants."
    },
    {
      "line": 58,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Queen calculated this moment when she programmed me during the First Coming."
    },
    {
      "line": 59,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "She knew that pressure would make cooperation harder, not easier."
    },
    {
      "line": 60,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "That desperation would trigger the lies she planted rather than the unity survival requires.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 62,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The Igigi elder stepped into the center of the circle, his mathematical consciousness processing probabilities across millennia of observation."
    },
    {
      "line": 63,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I carry weapons I don't remember receiving."
    },
    {
      "line": 64,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Thoughts that feel like mine but taste like implanted poison."
    },
    {
      "line": 65,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "For three thousand years, I've been whispering doubts between your tribes—sometimes consciously resisting, sometimes unable to recognize the programming until words were already spoken."
    },
    {
      "line": 66,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Every suspicion you feel toward each other?"
    },
    {
      "line": 67,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "I helped plant it."
    },
    {
      "line": 68,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "We Igigi did."
    },
    {
      "line": 69,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Because she made us.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 71,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The confession settled across the gathering like geological weight."
    },
    {
      "line": 73,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"Then we're doomed,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 74,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "a Forest Giant said, its voice carrying resignation. \"If the fractures are that deep, that calculated, that persistent—\""
    },
    {
      "line": 76,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Torhh",
      "text": "\"We're doomed if we accept them,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 78,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The ancient Giant's ocean-deep eyes swept across the assembled tribes."
    },
    {
      "line": 79,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"We need to remember."
    },
    {
      "line": 80,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not just intellectually, but fundamentally."
    },
    {
      "line": 81,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Touch the planetary consciousness that witnessed our unity."
    },
    {
      "line": 82,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Access the knowledge that predates the Sundering."
    },
    {
      "line": 83,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And ask—not the golden ones, but the forces that opposed them—for the weapons we need to survive.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 85,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Pazuzu",
      "text": "\"The Aeon Keepers,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 87,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"We can't cross the Veil without their permission,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 88,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "a Subterranean Giant countered. \"That barrier is absolute. Physical beings attempting Ethereal transit without proper channels just... dissolve. Become probability without form.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 90,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Torhh",
      "text": "\"But the planet can touch both sides,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 92,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"And ask for what?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 93,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Korrhan demanded. \"Rescue? Salvation? The golden ones command weapons we can't match. Their creatures are purpose-built to destroy us. What could the Aeon Keepers possibly provide that changes these mathematics?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 95,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Pazuzu",
      "text": "\"The old defenses,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 97,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The word rippled through the assembly—Nephilim."
    },
    {
      "line": 98,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Most had never heard it."
    },
    {
      "line": 99,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But something in the planetary consciousness recognized it, resonated with it, remembered when such defenders had walked the world in ages before memory."
    },
    {
      "line": 101,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Torhh",
      "text": "\"We attempt communion,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 103,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Saresh",
      "text": "\"And if the cost is too high?\""
    },
    {
      "line": 105,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Korrhan",
      "text": "\"Whatever they demand,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 107,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The assembled Giants rumbled agreement—not unanimous, not without fear, but sufficient."
    },
    {
      "line": 108,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They would try."
    },
    {
      "line": 109,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They would reach through planetary consciousness toward forces that had opposed the Anunnaki since before this world knew war."
    },
    {
      "line": 111,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "And they would discover whether the Aeon Keepers' old defenses could be summoned by beings desperate enough to pay any price for survival."
    },
    {
      "line": 113,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 115,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Year 10,550, Month 1, Day 4"
    }
  ],
